# Line-ending policy for the synthetic-data foundation.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The headline property of this dataset is that it regenerates byte-for-byte: run
# generator/generate_synthetic_data.py twice with the same seed and every one of the
# ~1,300 artifacts is identical. The generator writes LF explicitly.
#
# Git's autocrlf rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. Without this file, a fresh clone on
# Windows would land CRLF in the working tree, the first regeneration would rewrite
# every file back to LF, and `git status` would report all 1,300 artifacts as modified
# by someone who had done nothing but run the documented command.
#
# That turns the reproducibility guarantee into noise, and a guarantee that cries wolf
# is worse than none. So line endings are pinned to LF in the repository and in the
# working tree, on every platform.
#
# This file sits inside synthetic_data/ rather than at the repository root, matching
# the convention the validation suite already uses: gitattributes apply to their own
# subtree, and the root belongs to the CredPilot implementation.

# Every text artifact here is LF, in the repository and checked out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The completed research report is source evidence. It is quoted by 82 policy rules
# and its content should be byte-for-byte what was supplied, so it is exempted from
# conversion entirely rather than merely pinned.
research/deep-research-report.md -text
